  "slug": "optical-skyrmions-0cac",
  "summary": "New preprints show picosecond laser and spin-orbit-torque writing of skyrmions, antiferromagnetic textures and compensated states, plus probes of AFM switching.",
  "synthesis": "The main thread is deterministic writing of magnetic order with ultrafast optical or electrical stimuli. Picosecond circularly polarized pulses write fixed-chirality Néel skyrmions in Co/Pt, with chirality set by the Dzyaloshinskii-Moriya interaction. Laser pulses imprint antiferromagnetic skyrmions in a coupled ferromagnetic/antiferromagnetic bilayer within picoseconds. Atomistic simulations find all-optical helicity-independent switching in GdCo with as little as 1.5 at.% Gd. In triangular artificial spin ice, spin-orbit torque switching and planar Hall readout write and read a compensated state electrically. Two probe-oriented studies connect more loosely: pulsed-field MOKE up to 60 T on the metamagnetic transition in Fe2Mo3O8, and NV magnetometry of zero-field bistability and thermally activated switching in antiferromagnetic CrPS4 trilayers.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-23"
}
